cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  xeno-qpcr: Plasmodium 18S singleplex qPCR detection in blood-fed
  Anopheles gambiae sensu lato
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Atetteh
    given-names: Stephen
version: 1.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/stephenatetteh/xeno-qpcr
abstract: >-
  A Nextflow workflow taking raw QuantStudio exports of singleplex 18S rRNA
  TaqMan qPCR assays for Plasmodium falciparum, P. malariae and P. ovale
  through MIQE standard-curve and control quality control to zone-stratified
  prevalence estimates. The workflow validates that the plates which ran
  match the randomised sample-to-plate assignment, gates each control class
  separately, applies a documented calling rule in which trace is not
  positive, reports a cross-amplification sensitivity arm, and reports
  whether the randomisation decorrelated plate from collection site,
  bioclimatic zone, collection method and year.
keywords:
  - Plasmodium
  - Anopheles gambiae
  - qPCR
  - MIQE
  - Nextflow
  - malaria
  - vector biology
  - blood meal
references:
